 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and I suppose they will eat my flesh and drink my blood one day if they are as great as the great men of the town,\"",
  "[says] (to the second son) The eldest son says they are not as wealthy as the great men of the town.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Yes, my father, and we are not as wealthy as the great men of the town,\"",
  "[action] The second son laughs at the eldest son.",
  "[says] (to the second son) The eldest son says he wants to spend money on a house.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) speaks to eldest son",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what now?\"",
  "[action] The second son laughs again.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"I want to build a great house and have a fine courtyard and a garden and live like the rich men of the town.\"",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son laughs and says he will give his father a new courtyard.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"But this one has never been to a great house of a rich man except to borrow money from the great landowner,\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The second son laughs at the thought.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"It is not a thing to be feared,\"",
  "[silence] (to the second son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The second son turns to Wang Lung again.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"It is not the house that will be my end, but the money that I have in my hands and which will be lost if I do not spend it wisely.\"",
  "[action] The second son turns to his brother.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what is that to me?\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits on a bench.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and I have a little money left of my own and it is safe because it is in the land, and if I had it I would buy a little land for you in your own house, where I live,\""
